#
# Spellings removed from en_US.tsv because they are errors the corpus happened to contain, not
# words. Read by tools/drop_misspellings.py via --remove-list, and only ever applied to words
# that tool independently suspects, so a slip here cannot delete something it never flagged.
#
# Hand-checked, one at a time, and deliberately short. The detector finds 8,131 candidates and
# most of them must not be deleted: at every threshold measured it also proposes British
# spellings (collectables, hypothesised, practises), valid plurals (impedances, recognitions)
# and, in quantity, surnames the names pipeline missed (fong, leong, keyes, handley, eason).
# A rare surname and a typo are the same shape in this data -- a rare string one edit from a
# common word that no spell checker knows -- so the list is reviewed rather than generated.
#
# Two were considered and rejected as too risky for the gain:
#   calender   a real English word, a machine that presses paper. Hunspell does not hold it.
#   grammer    a surname, and hunspell does not hold that either.

teh          # the
recieve      # receive
seperate     # separate
adn          # and
thier        # their
occured      # occurred
beleive      # believe
becuase      # because
goverment    # government
alot         # not a word in any reading; "a lot" is two
